---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/astro/Navbar.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Exactly which cookies SWOTBee sets, who sets them, how long they last, and how to change or withdraw your choice at any time."
>
  <Navbar />
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-v6-bg to-white px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-16 pb-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-v6-dark mb-4">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-v6-text-muted">What we set, why, and how to change your mind.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-20">
    <p class="text-sm text-v6-text-muted"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 11 August 2026</p>

    <p class="mt-4">
      This policy explains which cookies and similar technologies swotbee.com uses, who
      sets them, how long they last, and how you control them. It describes what the site
      actually does today rather than what a website of this kind might typically do.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">1. Nothing optional runs until you say yes</h2>
    <p>
      When you first visit, analytics are switched off. A banner asks you to accept or
      reject analytics cookies, and both options are equally available. Until you accept:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-3 space-y-1">
      <li>No analytics or advertising cookies are stored on your device.</li>
      <li>Our session-recording tool is not loaded at all, so it cannot run.</li>
      <li>
        Google Analytics is told, before it loads, that consent is denied. In that state it
        sets no cookies and cannot identify you or recognise you across visits.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      One thing worth stating plainly, because most cookie policies leave it out: even
      before you choose, your browser still contacts Google to load the analytics tag,
      which means Google receives your IP address and the page address. No cookie is
      stored and no identifier is created. If you reject, that remains the case for the
      rest of your visit.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">2. Cookies we set</h2>
    <p>
      Durations are those set by the provider and can change when they update their own
      products.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Only after you accept analytics</h3>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="min-w-full mt-2 mb-6 text-sm border">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-v6-bg text-left">
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Name</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Set by</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Expires</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_ga</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Distinguishes one visitor from another so visits can be counted.</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Google Analytics 4</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_ga_*</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Keeps track of a single browsing session.</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Google Analytics 4</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_clck</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Links your activity on this site to a Microsoft Clarity identifier.</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Microsoft Clarity</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">1 year</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_clsk</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Joins several page views into one recorded session.</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Microsoft Clarity</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">1 day</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_gcl_au</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">
              Measures which advert led to an enquiry. Set only while we are running Google
              advertising.
            </td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Google Ads</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">90 days</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Microsoft Clarity records how pages are used, including mouse movement, scrolling and
      clicks, and can replay that as an anonymised session. We use it to find pages that
      confuse people. It is never loaded unless you accept.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Necessary, set regardless of your choice</h3>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="min-w-full mt-2 mb-6 text-sm border">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-v6-bg text-left">
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Name</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Set by</th>
            <th class="px-2 py-1 border">Expires</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>_GRECAPTCHA</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">
              Tells real people apart from bots when a form is submitted. Loaded only once
              you start filling in a form, not when you open the page.
            </td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Google reCAPTCHA</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">6 months</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border"><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">
              Blocks automated abuse of the booking calendar. Set only on our booking page,
              where a HubSpot scheduling tool is embedded.
            </td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">Cloudflare, via HubSpot</td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1 border">30 minutes</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      These protect the site from abuse and are not used to profile you or to measure
      traffic. Blocking them stops forms and the booking calendar from working.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Not a cookie</h3>
    <p>
      Your choice itself is kept in your browser's local storage under
      <code>sb_consent</code>, deliberately rather than in a cookie, so that remembering
      your answer does not itself require your permission. It never leaves your device.
      Clearing your browser data removes it, and the banner will ask again.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you arrive from an advertisement or a campaign link, the campaign details in that
      link are kept in your browser's session storage under <code>sb_attr</code> so that a
      form you submit a few pages later still tells us which campaign brought you here.
      It is first-party, is never shared with anyone for tracking, is deleted the moment
      you close the tab, and is only ever read to fill in a form you choose to send. If
      you never submit a form, it is never used for anything.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">3. Changing or withdrawing your choice</h2>
    <p>
      Select <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer of any page. The banner reopens
      and you can choose again. Withdrawing is as easy as consenting, and takes effect
      immediately.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you switch from accepted to rejected, we delete the analytics and advertising
      cookies listed above and reload the page, so the session-recording script is not
      running for the rest of your visit. We cannot delete data already collected and sent
      to Google or Microsoft before you withdrew. To ask about that data, contact us using
      the details below.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You can also block or delete cookies in your browser. Doing so applies to every site
      you visit, not just this one:
      <a class="text-v6-copper underline" href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Chrome</a>,
      <a class="text-v6-copper underline" href="https://support.mozilla.org/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Firefox</a>,
      <a class="text-v6-copper underline" href="https://support.apple.com/en-gb/guide/safari/sfri11471/mac" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Safari</a>,
      <a class="text-v6-copper underline" href="https://support.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Edge</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">4. What you lose by declining</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Every page, form, download and booking works exactly the same whether you
      accept or reject. Declining only means we cannot see which pages helped you, which
      makes the site slower to improve. That is our problem, not yours, which is why the
      reject button is the same size as the accept button.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">5. Who receives the data</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
      <li><strong>Google</strong> (Analytics, reCAPTCHA, and Ads when advertising is running)</li>
      <li><strong>Microsoft</strong> (Clarity, session analytics)</li>
      <li><strong>HubSpot</strong> (our CRM, for forms you submit and meetings you book)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These providers process data outside the UK and EU. How we handle the personal data
      you give us deliberately, such as your name and email in a form, is covered in our
      <a href="/privacy/" class="text-v6-copper underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">6. Other tracking technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Our marketing emails may contain a tracking pixel that records whether the email was
      opened and which links were selected. That is separate from this site and is governed
      by the consent you gave when subscribing. Every email includes an unsubscribe link.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">7. Updates to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We update this page when what we use changes, and revise the date at the top. If we
      add a tracking technology that needs consent, it will be off by default and the
      banner will ask you again.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">8. Contact</h2>
    <address class="not-italic">
      <p>
        Email: <a href="mailto:support@swotbee.com" class="text-v6-copper underline">support@swotbee.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>SWOTBee</p>
      <p>Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India</p>
    </address>
  </section>
</Layout>
